apple just made it extremely difficult  to choose which apple watch to buy  because they've not only added the brand  new ultra model into the lineup for the  first time ever but they've also reduced  the price of the apple watch se while  barely making any changes to the series  8. so in this video i'm going to stop  all of the confusion and explain all of  the main differences between them to  help you decide which apple watch to buy  and i'm going to give you guys some  advice that you're probably not  expecting so without further ado let's  jump right into it starting with the  biggest difference between all three  models the materials and sizes the apple  watch sc starts at 249 dollars and only  comes in aluminum in either midnight  starlight or silver with the smallest  case sizes either 40 or 44 millimeters  for 150 dollars more you can get the new  series 8 which comes in aluminum for the  base price and it gets an extra color  option product red and slightly larger  41 and 45 millimeter case sizes however  you can also get the series 8 in  stainless steel in either graphite  silver or gold but you'll have to pay at  least seven hundred dollars for these  and the price continues to go up based  on the band that you like and then  finally we have the brand new apple  watch ultra which is priced at the same  800  no matter which one of the new extreme  sports bands you choose which actually  makes it a killer value as i'm gonna  show you guys in just a minute but the  main thing you need to know is that it  only comes in the natural finish with  the now exclusive titanium chassis and  the massive 49 millimeter case size  which might actually be too large for  some people out there just look at this  side by side comparison right here as  well as how huge it looks on ijustine's  wrist now before this watch launched  there were some rumors floating around  saying that the existing watch bands  would not be compatible with this new  ultra model but thankfully you can also  use any 42 to 45 millimeter apple watch  band and that's actually perfect because  our sponsor juke sent us over some  custom made and designed apple watch  bands that are probably the highest  quality bands i've seen with stainless  steel butterfly clasps even on this one  which uses genuine italian leather from  a tannery in florence and the aluminum  bands like this onyx chrono are  extremely high quality yet incredibly  light including this ruby red vituro  band with custom engineered tapered  links for perfect curvature around the  wrist and juke even includes tools in  the box for adjustment with great  options for the ladies as well so check  them out in the description below now  getting back to the apple watch  differences the ultra has the biggest  display size and pixel density and it's  the only one that features a completely  flat sapphire crystal glass panel that's  actually protected by the titanium lip  compared to the other models with curved  and exposed glass the ultra also comes  with a completely unique design that's  rounded at first but then gets flat  towards the display and on the left side  it gets a new orange action button which  is customizable and unique to the ultra  while also featuring this large crown  guard that sticks out of the side  protecting the larger beefier crown and  this actually helps apple save room on  the inside of the watch itself allowing  apple to pack in a battery that's 76  percent larger than the one in the  series 8. and that leads to 36 hours of  battery life exactly double the amount  you get with both the series 8 and the  new se but it also makes the watch about  35 thicker than the other two and  surprisingly it's almost two times  heavier than the 44 millimeter se model  and about 19 heavier than the stainless  steel series 8. now believe it or not  but they all feature the same s8 chip  which is actually a rebranded s7 which  was already a rebranded s6 which is kind  of funny but i guess it means the chips  are fast enough for everything these  watches need to do the only difference  is that the se model doesn't come with  the u1 ultra wide band chip for precise  device tracking the se also doesn't get  features like the blood oxygen sensor  the electrical heart sensor the third  generation optical heart sensor fast  charging support the brand new  temperature sensing feature which is  available on both of the other models  for ovulation tracking ip6x  dust resistance and of course the se  doesn't get the always on display but to  be honest it still packs a majority of  the major features like car crash  detection 32 gigs of storage sleep  tracking support for the new compass and  backtrack features and more all for only  250 dollars and even more shocking you  only need to pay 50 dollars more to  upgrade to the cellular model making it  the absolute best choice if you're  buying an apple watch for your kid  instead of a more expensive iphone but  now let's dig into some of the things  that you can only get on the ultra  because it's really quite impressive  since this is meant to be an extreme  sports apple watch the ultra comes with  a display that can reach up to a massive  2000 nits of brightness which will  basically make the display easily  readable while in direct sunlight and it  also has the best water resistance at up  to 100 meters compared to 50 on the  other two in terms of durability and  weather proofing it's tested to the 810  h military standard and it's also the  only one that is certified for diving up  to 40 meters deep with the en  13319 certification which is the best  rating out there making it qualify as a  legit diving computer and apple even  gives you the exclusive oceanic plus  diving app for that alongside the new  depth gauge and water temperature sensor  features it also comes with precision  dual frequency gps with the added l5  band and it gets a new dual speaker  setup which is 40 louder than on the  series 8 allowing for the new siren  feature which i'm personally excited for  and it also gets a new 3 mic array with  beam forming for the best microphone  quality you can get it's also the only  apple watch that comes with bluetooth  5.3 to match the new iphone 14s and the  airpods pro 2 and of course it comes  with cellular built in at the base 800  price which i have to admit makes it the  best bang for the buck apple watch model  out there thanks to the massive 36 hours  of battery life and together with the  new low power mode the ultra can go up  to 60 hours on a single charge which is  actually really impressive and as a  little bonus it also gets a unique  braided usbc charging cable inside of  the really creative and high quality  packaging but now with all those  differences out of the way it's time to  get into my personal buyer's advice for  all of you guys out there including some  advice that you probably are not  expecting to hear from me if you're  currently looking at the series 8 apple  watch i would honestly recommend that  you stop and instead buy the series 7 on  amazon since you can find a renewed  model for as low as 317  or a brand new 45 millimeter model with  cellular for only 400 bucks and the  reason i'm making that recommendation is  because the series 8 really only has two  advantages over the seven it comes with  the car crash detection feature and  ovulation tracking and if that doesn't  matter that much to you then simply go  for the series seven now if you're  looking to spend even less cash like  let's say you're buying someone in apple  watch as a gift then the new se is  probably going to be the best option  since it packs most of the important  features for an incredibly low 250  dollar price however keep in mind that  it doesn't have an always on display  which might be important for the person  you're buying it for but let's say  you're buying it for a kid in that case  it's not gonna matter and it's a hundred  percent the model that i recommend for  kids but be sure to pay the extra fifty  dollars for the cellular model because  it's required for the kids setup feature  and then finally we have the ultra which  is in my opinion by far the best bang  for your buck in terms of how feature  packed and rugged it is especially with  double the battery life which is  basically the most important thing in  any battery-powered device it's also  something that's completely fresh and  new so it's probably going to be an  exciting choice for those who are  getting kind of bored of the general  apple watch design like myself and  that's honestly why i bought it but just  keep in mind that the 49 millimeter  chassis might look a little bit too big  for people with smaller wrists so you  might want to try it out at a nearby  apple store first if you live close to  one so there you guys go hopefully this  video helped you make a decision on  which apple watch model to buy and if it  did definitely check out juke's premium  apple watch bands down in the  description below and go ahead and click  the circle above to subscribe for our  hands-on comparison videos coming up  this weekend and check out one of those  two videos right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  one  [Music]  you

